IG with a TSIG whose algorithm string is not recognized by the library should cause an IllegalArgumentException. This tests the algorithm validation branch inside setTSIG.'}]}, {'group': 'Duplicate TSIG record already present', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'key', 'value': 'new TSIG(Name.fromString("dup.example.com."), "hmac-sha256", "dGVzdFNlY3JldA==")'}], 'expected': 'IllegalStateException thrown', 'description': "If a TSIGRecord is already present in the message's additional section (added via addRecord), a subsequent call to setTSIG should reject the operation and throw IllegalStateException, preventing multiple TSIGs."}]}, {'group': 'Null TSIG key after message already contains TSIGRecord', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'key', 'value': 'null'}], 'expected': 'IllegalArgumentException thrown', 'description': 'Even when a TSIGRecord already exists in the message, passing a null key to setTSIG must still trigger the null‑check and throw IllegalArgumentException.'}]}, {'group': 'TSIG key with null name', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'key', 'value': 'new TSIG(null, "hmac-sha256", "dGVzdFNlY3JldA==")'}], 'expected': 'NullPointerException thrown', 'description': 'Constructing a TSIG with a null Name is illegal; setTSIG should propagate the NullPointerException thrown by the TSIG constructor.'}]}]
